Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.990 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  apigee x allows you to expose your apis  to end users by implementing api proxies  away proxies are nothing but a wrapper  for your actual apis  did you know that the api proxy must be  deployed for it to be invoked  the process of deploying the ebay proxy  and making it accessible to the end  users is referred to as api proxy  deployment before you deploy your api  proxy you need to complete a set of  prerequisites correctly  networking and routing configurations  are two of the key prerequisites for api  proxy deployment  a key point to note if the  configurations are not defined correctly  then your api proxies may not be  accessible  in this video we will learn the apigee x  networking architecture and demonstrate  how to verify the networking  configuration of an apigee x  organization on high level there are  three key things to be configured in  networking  first the virtual private clouds ovpcs  apigex instances are provisioned in  internal google managed vpcs  however google managed vpcs are not  directly accessible from your gcp  projects  therefore you need to pair them either  with vpcs or shared vpcs created in your  gcp projects  secondly the manage instance group omig  currently gcp load balances cannot  directly route requests to google manage  vpcs  therefore you need to use a mig for 14  requests received by the load balancer  to the apigee x instance  be aware that this mig needs to be  created in the same vpc network attached  to the apigee ex organization and an  ingress firewall rule is required for  allowing the load balancer to route  request to the mig  finally the load balancer  depending on your routing requirements  you could either choose an external or  an internal load balancer for routing  requests to the apigee x instances  keep in mind that if you are using a  shared vpc then ensure that all manage  instance groups client hos and target  hosts are created in the same network as  shown in this diagram  alright  let's jump into the google cloud console  and verify the networking configuration  in a sample apigee x organization  first off let's verify if the proper vpc  network is attached to a sample apigee x  organization  open the cloud shell  execute the following api request to  determine the vpc network attached to  the apigex organization  the authorized network property in this  output refers to the name of the  attached vpc  if you are using a shared vpc ensure  that authorized network property has the  name of the actual vpc that is attached  to the gcp project in which the load  balancer and the mig's are created  next up to verify the configuration of  the mig  go to compute engine instance groups  page and select your mig  click on the instance template scroll  down to the network tags section and  note down the tags  next  ensure the vpc network defined in the  network interfaces section is the same  as the vpc attached to the apigee x  organization  scroll down further to the custom  metadata section and verify the endpoint  ip address against the apigee x instance  ip address  navigate to the vpc network firewall  page and verify the ingress firewall  rule  be aware this firewall rule needs to be  created in the same vpc attached to the  apigee x organization  ensure that the network tags of the mig  are defined under target tags  and allow the load balancer healthcheck  probes source ip addresses ranges are  included under the source filters  section  finally let's look at how to verify the  load balancer configuration  go to network services load balancing  and click on the load balancer name  under the front end section verify that  protocol ip address port and the tls  certificate are configured correctly  next if any host and path rules are  defined verify whether they are  configured correctly  lastly under the backline section verify  that the load balancer backend is  healthy and it is pointing to the right  mig which forwards traffic to the apogex  instance to summarize you learn the  networking architecture in apigee x and  how to verify the networking  configuration  namely vpc mig and load balancers are  configured correctly in an apigee ex  organization  [Music]

